Submission details

Create your 4-page paper using this template.
You must follow the template and following list of guidelines very strictly or your submission will be ineligible:

do not edit the TeX document preamble (i.e., the code before \begin{document} must not be changed);
do not use external .bib-files;
do not alter/add additional packages;
do not create personal definitions/commands (e.g., using \newcommand or \def);
do not change the font size; do write the paper in English;
do use cross-references unique to the first author’s name, e.g., \label{johnsmith:likelihood};
do rename the template file to make it identifiable following the format FirstAuthor_ShortPaperTitle.tex.

To ensure proper evaluation, short papers should be approximately (but no more than) 4 pages for the initial submission.
We encourage authors to submit their figures in colors. However, wherever possible, efforts should be made to produce figures which are meaningfully readable also under black-and-white print.

After creating your 4-page short paper with the provided style files, you must submit using the Online Paper Submission Form. Note that:

papers submitted as an Oral Presentation will be considered as either an oral presentation OR a poster presentation (as the total number of accepted oral presentations is limited),
papers submitted as a Poster Presentation will be considered ONLY as poster presentation.

Once your paper has been submitted successfully, you will receive a confirmation email. If you do not receive this email, please check your junk/spam folder.
Your submitted paper will be reviewed by members of the IWSM 2027 Scientific Committee and the outcome of this review will be provided by 31.03.2027.
Following the review, accepted papers may be extended to 6 pages. For this final accepted version, we will need a .zip file containing all files necessary to compile your manuscript for inclusion into the IWSM 2027 Proceedings Volume. This will be an online PDF file that ultimately resides on the Statistical Modelling Society website.
Legal considerations: Authors grant the IWSM 2027 organisers the right to publish their accepted contribution in the conference proceedings. However, copyright will always remain with the authors, who are free to publish the same material elsewhere after the workshop. It is the responsibility of the authors to ensure that publication in the conference proceedings does not conflict with any other pre-existing agreements.
